---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import MedicalDisclaimer from '../components/MedicalDisclaimer.astro';
import FormattedDate from '../components/FormattedDate.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import authorPhoto from '../assets/denis-ethier.png';
import { sortPostsDescending } from '../utils/postUtils';

const rawPosts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
// Show posts relevant for dental practitioners
const dentistPosts = sortPostsDescending(rawPosts).filter(post => {
	const tags = post.data.tags || [];
	return tags.includes('clinician') || tags.includes('both');
});
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead 
			title="For Dentists | Decoding The Burn" 
			description="How dentists and periodontists can collaborate with patient-led time-series data to discover clinical blind spots in Burning Mouth Syndrome." 
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<!-- Hero Section Following Homepage Model -->
			<section class="hero-centered-wrapper">
				<div class="hero-centered-header">
					<MedicalDisclaimer />
					<h1 class="hero-centered-title">
						How Dentists Can Use This&nbsp;Site
					</h1>
					<p class="hero-centered-subtitle">
						When patients present with 10/10 oral burning and pristine pink mucosa, conventional exams reach their limits.
						Here is how dense, longitudinal dental and pH data can help uncover hidden root&nbsp;triggers.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Video on Top -->
				<div class="hero-video-centered">
					<div class="video-placeholder-wrapper" style="cursor: default;">
						<Image 
							src={authorPhoto} 
							alt="Denis Ethier - BMS Dental Orientation Video" 
							class="video-placeholder-img" 
							width={1400} 
							height={788} 
						/>
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Message to Dentists Card Under Video -->
				<article class="personal-story-section">
					<h2 class="story-heading">My Experience &amp; A Message to Dental Practitioners</h2>
					<div class="story-lead">
						<p class="story-paragraph">
							I am a Burning Mouth Syndrome patient who lived through three years of debilitating 10/10 oral burning. 
							During that time, I sat in the chairs of five dentists and periodontists. Every practitioner was diligent, 
							kind, and genuinely wanted to help me. Yet every examination concluded the same way: 
							<em>"Your mucosa looks healthy and pink. There are no lesions, no infections, and no obvious pathology."</em>
						</p>
						<p class="story-paragraph">
							Because I come from an engineering and software architecture background, I couldn't accept that 
							severe physical pain had no physical origin. I began treating my oral cavity like an interconnected biomechanical system. 
							What I discovered through meticulous self-tracking was a critical blind spot in modern dental workflows: 
							<strong>the compound effect of subgingival tartar pockets, localized gingival recession, mechanical composite shielding, and acidic micro-leakage.</strong>
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="story-body-grid">
						<div class="story-card">
							<div class="story-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<path d="M12 2v20M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"></path>
								</svg>
							</div>
							<h3 class="story-card-title">1. Time-Series Data vs. Single-Point Snapshots</h3>
							<p class="story-card-text">
								Standard dental appointments are 30-minute point-in-time snapshots. But Burning Mouth Syndrome is a dynamic, 
								time-series condition with 48-to-72-hour biochemical latencies. Dense daily logs capture the exact trajectory 
								between subgingival calculus removal, acidic exposure, and mucosal flare-ups.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="story-card">
							<div class="story-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
									<line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
									<line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
								</svg>
							</div>
							<h3 class="story-card-title">2. Subgingival Pockets &amp; Perioscopy</h3>
							<p class="story-card-text">
								Blind tactile probing often misses microscopic burnished calculus and biofilm trapped in deep 4-5mm pockets. 
								Using subgingival micro-endoscopy (perioscopy) allows direct visual validation of root surfaces that can ignite 
								trigeminal nerve branches without overt soft tissue ulceration.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="story-card">
							<div class="story-card-icon" aria-hidden="true">
								<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
									<path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z"></path>
								</svg>
							</div>
							<h3 class="story-card-title">3. Cervical Bonding &amp; Dentin Shielding</h3>
							<p class="story-card-text">
								In my case, placing 4 cervical composite bonding patches over exposed root recession provided 6 months of complete 
								pain-free relief by creating a physical shield against salivary acids, demonstrating a direct mechanical-chemical link.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Direct Collaboration CTA -->
					<div class="collab-cta-box">
						<h3 class="collab-cta-title">Are you a dental professional seeing BMS in your practice?</h3>
						<p class="collab-cta-text">
							I am actively collaborating with open-minded dentists, periodontists, and oral medicine specialists to build 
							reproducible diagnostic checklists and interview specialists on the podcast.
						</p>
						<div class="collab-cta-actions">
							<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
							<a href="/podcast/guest-guide" class="btn btn-secondary">Guest Guide for Dentists</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- Casebook Articles Section -->
				<section class="patient-articles-section">
					<div class="section-heading-wrapper">
						<h2 class="section-title">Dental &amp; Clinical Case Studies</h2>
						<p class="section-subtitle">
							In-depth technical breakdowns of dental hardware, calculus imaging, pH mechanics, and periodontal interventions.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="articles-grid">
						{dentistPosts.map((post) => (
							<article class="article-card">
								<a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`} class="article-card-link">
									{post.data.heroImage && (
										<div class="article-image-wrapper">
											<img 
												src={post.data.heroImage} 
												alt={post.data.title} 
												class="article-image" 
												loading="lazy"
											/>
										</div>
									)}
									<div class="article-content">
										<div class="article-meta">
											<span class="article-category">{post.data.category || 'Clinical'}</span>
											<span class="meta-separator">•</span>
											<span class="article-date"><FormattedDate date={post.data.pubDate} /></span>
										</div>
										<h3 class="article-title">{post.data.title}</h3>
										<p class="article-desc">{post.data.description}</p>
									</div>
								</a>
							</article>
						))}
					</div>
				</section>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.hero-centered-wrapper {
		max-width: 1100px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
	}

	.hero-centered-header {
		text-align: center;
		max-width: 780px;
		margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
	}

	.hero-centered-title {
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.15;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin: 1.25rem 0 1rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.hero-centered-subtitle {
		font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.hero-video-centered {
		max-width: 900px;
		margin: 0 auto 3rem;
		border-radius: 20px;
		overflow: hidden;
		box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
		background: #000000;
	}

	.video-placeholder-wrapper {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
	}

	.video-placeholder-img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		opacity: 0.95;
	}

	.personal-story-section {
		background: var(--bg-card, #ffffff);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e2e8f0);
		border-radius: 24px;
		padding: 3rem 2.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 4rem;
		box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
	}

	.story-heading {
		font-size: 1.85rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		text-align: center;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.story-lead {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
	}

	.story-paragraph {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.story-body-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.story-card {
		background: #f8fafc;
		border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
		border-radius: 16px;
		padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
	}

	.story-card-icon {
		color: #991b1b;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.story-card-title {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.story-card-text {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.collab-cta-box {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e1136 0%, #0d081a 100%);
		border-radius: 18px;
		padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
		text-align: center;
		color: #ffffff;
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3);
	}

	.collab-cta-title {
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.collab-cta-text {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #e2e8f0;
		max-width: 620px;
		margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.collab-cta-actions {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}

	.patient-articles-section {
		margin-top: 3rem;
	}

	.section-heading-wrapper {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
	}

	.section-title {
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.section-subtitle {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		max-width: 600px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.articles-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.article-card {
		background: #ffffff;
		border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
		border-radius: 16px;
		overflow: hidden;
		transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
	}

	.article-card:hover {
		transform: translateY(-4px);
		box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
	}

	.article-card-link {
		text-decoration: none;
		color: inherit;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		height: 100%;
	}

	.article-image-wrapper {
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.article-image {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.article-content {
		padding: 1.5rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		flex: 1;
	}

	.article-meta {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: #64748b;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.article-category {
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #991b1b;
	}

	.article-title {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.3;
		color: var(--text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.article-desc {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.personal-story-section {
			padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
		}
	}
</style>
